# in the sibling finalist_selection/ directory, which stay tracked.
isles26_project/workspace/results/ensemble_tmp
# ensemble_test.py's --work-dir: same reasoning -- scratch ensembled masks for
# the held-out (test_id/test_ood) scoring pass, rewritten every run, never a
# deliverable (the real output is workspace/results/runs/ensemble_*/results_test.csv).
isles26_project/workspace/results/ensemble_test_tmp

# Hidden final-holdout test set (id + ood) -- this project's stand-in for the
# real, never-received ISLES'26 challenge test set. Must never be committed or
# casually inspected; also self-.gitignore's via its own .gitignore. See
# data_prep/split_dataset.py and CLAUDE.md.
**/final_holdout/
# ...except: let the isles26_project final_holdout/ directory itself register
# in git (via a tracked .gitkeep) so the folder's existence is visible in the
# repo structure -- e.g. to Claude via the GitHub connector -- without
# un-hiding any of its contents. The dir's own .gitignore ("*", with a
# !.gitkeep exception) still blocks every real file underneath.
!isles26_project/workspace/final_holdout/

